              "settings": { "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": { "unit": "px", "size": 8 }, "_column_size": 70 },
              "elements": [
                {
                  "id": "1000087",
                  "elType": "widget",
                  "widgetType": "heading",
                  "settings": { "title": "Business scenario", "header_size": "h4", "title_color": "#14151A" },
                  "elements": []
                },
                {
                  "id": "1000088",
                  "elType": "widget",
                  "widgetType": "text-editor",
                  "settings": { "editor": "<p>NorthWind Retail, a mid-size online retailer, exports daily CSV files of orders and order line items from its e-commerce platform. The analytics team wants per-category revenue and a top-5 best-selling products report every morning, but some rows in the daily export are broken (missing unit price, zero/negative quantity, or an order_item pointing at an order_id that does not exist), and the file has grown too large to comfortably explore in a spreadsheet or plain pandas on a laptop. The data engineering team is introducing Apache Spark so the same logic will still work when the daily export grows from thousands to millions of rows.</p>", "text_color": "#54575F" },
                  "elements": []
                },
                {
                  "id": "1000089",
                  "elType": "widget",
                  "widgetType": "heading",
                  "settings": { "title": "Deliverable", "header_size": "h4", "title_color": "#14151A" },
                  "elements": []
                },
                {
                  "id": "1000090",
                  "elType": "widget",
                  "widgetType": "text-editor",
                  "settings": { "editor": "<p>A PySpark script (analyze_orders.py) that reads orders.csv and order_items.csv, filters out invalid line items, joins orders to their line items, computes total revenue per product category, computes the top 5 products by revenue, and writes both results to CSV files, verified by an automated pytest suite that runs Spark in local mode.</p>", "text_color": "#54575F" },
                  "elements": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "1000091",
              "elType": "container",
              "isInner": true,
              "settings": { "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": { "unit": "px", "size": 8 }, "_column_size": 30, "flex_justify_content": "center" },
              "elements": [
                {
                  "id": "1000092",
                  "elType": "widget",
